  "extracted_on": "2026-10-13",
  "method": "Shallow git clone; the sniff files were parsed as text with a Python script: every HTMLCS.addMessage(...) call was located with a parenthesis-depth scanner, the first argument gave the level (literal constant, a local variable resolved from its assignments in the enclosing method, or a method parameter attributed to the wrapper sniff that passes a literal level) and the fourth argument gave the code (string literal, a code variable resolved from its base assignments and += suffixes, or a line-checked manual table for the H49.<Tag> and H91.<Control> patterns). Ruleset membership comes from the include list in Standards/WCAG2AA/ruleset.js, which the engine uses verbatim as the sniff list (HTMLCS.js _registerStandard). Counts are call sites, not run-time occurrences.",
  "wcag_version": "WCAG 2.1 (README.markdown links https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG21/; ruleset description 'Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 AA'; sniffs exist for the 2.1-only criteria 1.3.4, 1.3.5, 1.4.10-1.4.13, 2.1.4, 2.5.1-2.5.6 and 4.1.3; no WCAG 2.2 criteria such as 2.4.11, 2.5.7, 2.5.8, 3.2.6, 3.3.7 or 3.3.8)",
  "message_levels": {
    "ERROR": 1,
    "WARNING": 2,
    "NOTICE": 3
  },
  "sniff_files_total": 80,
  "sniffs_in_wcag2aa": 52,
  "addmessage_call_sites_total": 200,
  "caveats": [
    "Counts are addMessage call sites by level, not the number of distinct codes and not run-time message counts.",
    "1_3_1.js line 159 chooses ERROR or WARNING at run time; it is counted once under each level.",
    "The two G141 heading-order call sites in 1_3_1.js take their level from the caller, so they are counted under 1_3_1_A.js (WARNING, used by WCAG2A and WCAG2AA) and 1_3_1_AAA.js (ERROR, used by WCAG2AAA), not under 1_3_1.js.",
    "1_4_3_Contrast.js is a helper object with no register() or messages; the WCAG2AA ruleset still lists it. 1_4_3.js (4.5:1 / 3:1) and 1_4_6.js (7:1 / 4.5:1) call its testContrastRatio() and emit the messages.",
    "4_1_2.js builds H91.<Control>.Name and H91.<Control>.Value codes from element names at run time; they are listed as H91.*.Name and H91.*.Value.",
    "2_5_2.js and 2_5_4.js pass an empty code string to addMessage; it is listed as \"\".",
    "A sniff file 1_2_3.js exists, but only the WCAG2A ruleset includes it; the WCAG2AA and WCAG2AAA rulesets omit it (1.2.5 audio description covers 1.2.3 at AA). Likewise WCAG2AAA omits 2.2.1, 2.3.1, 2.4.4, 3.3.4 and 1_4_3 in favour of the stricter AAA criteria.",
    "No sniff files exist for 2.1.3 and 2.4.10 (AAA); no messages are defined for them.",
    "The level constants are HTMLCS.ERROR = 1, HTMLCS.WARNING = 2, HTMLCS.NOTICE = 3 (HTMLCS.js lines 28-30)."
  ],
